+**Updates from GitHub Releases.** `.github/workflows/release.yml` runs on every push to `main`.
+When `VERSION` has no GitHub release yet, it builds the macOS app (`GameDevWorkstation-<v>-macos-arm64.zip`
+and `.dmg`) and the Windows installer (`GameDevWorkstation-<v>-x64-setup.exe`) and publishes them as
+release `v<version>`. Those builds carry the `github` update channel (`GDW_UPDATE_CHANNEL=github` and
+`GDW_UPDATE_REPO` when `scripts/version.py build-info` runs). About every 6 hours, and on **Check now**,
+they read the repo's latest release. If it's newer, they download the asset for their platform into the
+updates folder (`<dir>/<version>/` with a `release.json`, then `latest.json`), and the folder updater above
+takes it from there. Local builds (`make app`, `make release`, running from source) never call GitHub.
+
+**Automatic install.** With `[updates] auto_install = true` (the default), the app installs a pending
+update by itself once no session is running a turn. Each version is tried once, so an install that
+fails doesn't loop; **Install & restart** still works by hand. Set it to `false` to only be offered updates.
+
+**Windows.** A Windows release is the installer. Installing hands over to a PowerShell helper that
+stops the app, runs the installer silently (`/S`) and starts the app again. The log is
+`update.log` in the app's logs folder. Rollback isn't available on Windows.
+
 **First install.** An app built before this feature can't update itself. Install once by
 hand, then updates arrive in-app:
 
